Let ${\Delta} > 1$, $k\geq 1$ and $N>1$ be integers, $c>0$, $\uprho> 1$, $\darkmagenta{s}\geq 1$, while let $b,\varepsilon\in (0,1)$. Also, let $ eta,\gamma, \lambda\in \mathbb{R}$ be such that $\gamma >0$, $0\leq  eta\leq \gamma$ and $\lambda>0$. Consider graph $G=(V,E)$ of maximum degree ${\Delta}$ such that $
norm{ (\cadmiumgreen{\UpH}_{G,k})^N}{1/N}{2}= \uprho$. Assume that $\mu$, the Gibbs distribution on $G$ specified by the parameters $( eta, \gamma, \lambda)$, is $b$-marginally bounded. For $\delta=  rac{1-\varepsilon}{\uprho}$, suppose that there is a $(\darkmagenta{s},\delta,c)$-potential function ${\Psi}$ with respect to $( eta,\gamma,\lambda)$. There are constants $\ell_0> 2k$, $\widehat{x}_1\geq 1$ such that, for $\Lambda\subset V$ and $	au\in \{\pm 1\}^{\Lambda}$, for any $u,w\in V\setminus \Lambda$ with ${m dist}(u,w)\geq 2k$ and walk $P\in \iris{{\mathcal{E}}}_{\Lambda,k}$ that emanates from $w$, the following is true: For $\ell\geq \ell_0$, for path $W=e_1, \ldots, e_{\ell}$ from the root of $\overline{\cadmiumgreen{T}}=T_{m SAW}(\gext{G}{P}, u)$ to a copy of vertex $w$, we have  egin{align}
onumber \prod
olimits_{1\leq i \leq \ell} \abs{\upalpha_{P}(e_{i})} & \leq \widehat{x}_1 \cdot (1+\varepsilon/3)^{\ell/\darkmagenta{s}} \cdot \prod
olimits_{1\leq i\leq \ell-k} \abs{\upalpha (e_{i})} \enspace. \end{align}

Let ${\Delta}> 1$ and $k> 0$, let $ eta,\gamma, \lambda, b \in \mathbb{R}$ be such that $\gamma >0$, $0\leq  eta\leq \gamma, \lambda>0$ and $b>0$. Let $G=(V,E)$ be of maximum degree ${\Delta}$. Consider $\mu_G$ the Gibbs distribution on $G$ specified by the parameters $( eta, \gamma, \lambda)$, while assume that $\mu_G$ is $b$-marginally bounded. There are constants $C_1, C_2>0$ such that, for any $\Lambda\subset V$ and any $	au\in \{\pm 1\}^{\Lambda}$, we have  egin{align}
onumber 
orm{ {\mathcal{I}}^{\Lambda,	au}_G}{2} \leq C_1+ C_2 \cdot 
orm{ \abs{\applegreen{{\mathcal{L}}}^{\Lambda,	au}_{G,k}}}{2} \enspace. \end{align}

Let $\delta, b \in \mathbb{R}_{>0}$ and integers ${\Delta}, k\geq 1$. Also, let $ eta,\gamma, \lambda\in \mathbb{R}$ be such that $0\leq  eta\leq \gamma$, $\gamma >0$ and $\lambda>0$. Consider graph $G=(V,E)$ of maximum degree ${\Delta}$ while assume that $\mu_G$, the Gibbs distribution on $G$ specified by the parameters $( eta, \gamma, \lambda)$, is $b$-marginally bounded. Suppose the set of functions $\{ H_d\}_{1\leq d< {\Delta}}$ specified by $( eta,\gamma,\lambda)$ exhibits $\delta$-contraction. There are constants $C_1,C_2>0$ such that, for any $\Lambda\subset V$ and $	au\in \{\pm 1\}^{\Lambda}$, the influence matrix ${\mathcal{I}}^{\Lambda,	au}_{G}$, induced by $\mu^{\Lambda,	au}_G$, satisfies  egin{align}
onumber 
orm{ {\mathcal{I}}^{\Lambda,	au}_{G}}{2} &\leq C_1+C_2 \cdot \sum
olimits_{\ell\geq k} \delta^{\ell} \cdot 
orm{ ( \cadmiumgreen{\UpH}_{G,k})^{\ell}}{2} \enspace . \end{align}

We have  egin{align} 
orm{ \mathcal{J}}{2} &\leq \sum 
olimits_{\ell\geq k} \delta^{\ell+k} \cdot 
orm{ ( \cadmiumgreen{\UpH}_{G,k} )^{\ell}}{2} \enspace. \end{align}

Let ${\Delta} > 1$ and $k,N\geq 1$ be integers, $c>0$, $\uprho> 1$, $\darkmagenta{s}\geq 1$ while let $b,\varepsilon\in (0,1)$. Also, let $ eta,\gamma, \lambda\in \mathbb{R}$ be such that $\gamma >0$, $0\leq  eta\leq \gamma$ and $\lambda>0$. Consider graph $G=(V,E)$ of maximum degree ${\Delta}$ such that $
norm{ (\cadmiumgreen{\UpH}_{G,k})^N}{1/N}{2}= \uprho$. Assume that $\mu_G$, the Gibbs distribution on $G$ specified by the parameters $( eta, \gamma, \lambda)$, is $b$-marginally bounded. For $\delta=  rac{1-\varepsilon}{\uprho}$, suppose that there is a $(\darkmagenta{s},\delta,c)$-potential function ${\Psi}$ with respect to $( eta,\gamma,\lambda)$. There exists a fixed constant $\widehat{c} \geq 1$ such that for any $\Lambda\subset V$ and $	au\in \{\pm 1\}^{\Lambda}$, the extended influence matrix $\applegreen{{\mathcal{L}}}^{\Lambda,	au}_{G,k}$, that is induced by $\mu^{\Lambda,	au}_G$, satisfies that  egin{align}
onumber 
orm{ \abs{ \applegreen{{\mathcal{L}}}^{\Lambda,	au}_{G,k}}}{2\darkmagenta{s}} &\leq \widehat{c}\cdot \sum
olimits_{\ell\geq k} \left( {	extstyle \left( rac{1-\varepsilon/2}{\uprho}ight)^{\ell} } \cdot 
orm{ ( \cadmiumgreen{\UpH}_{G,k})^{\ell}}{2} ight)^{1/\darkmagenta{s}} \enspace. \end{align}

For any $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$, $d>0$, $R > 1$ and $ eta\in {\mathbb{U}_{m Ising}}(R,\varepsilon )$ we have {\small  egin{align} \sup
